Not Another Unintended Side-effect of the Eating Add-ons ...

i don't think this particular aspect of eating behavior got reported:
you could and can still eat a dragon corpse safely if you're not
satiated and don't get interrupted while eating. during the process you
may get a message stating that you're having a hard time getting it all
down but it is of no consequence. under the new eating code (HARD 4.3
BSD Unix nethack 3.0g patchlevel 5 with stopgap) if you attempt to eat
a dragon corpse while not satiated and get interrupted you may notice
the following:
1) you are carrying a complete dragon corpse (in your inventory) which
    is normally impossible. you collapse under load when you move.
2) you are satiated even though the dragon corpse appears to be intact
    and not partly eaten.
3) if you resume eating you will promptly choke over your food which is
    inconsistent with the fact that if you don't get interrupted you can
    safely eat a dragon corpse.
4) if you were wearing an amulet of life saving at the time, the amulet
    will save you but then you automatically continue to eat and promptly
    choke again rendering the amulet useless in this case.

as seen above, there are a number of troubling problems with this behavior.
the "stable" version of 3.0 should, at least, fix these problems.
